<h2>Sources and further reading</h2>
<p>Checked against PostgreSQL 18 documentation on 25 October 2026. Native observations use PostgreSQL 18.6 on Linux/aarch64 in an isolated disposable instance; the generated fixture retains all core shop rows. The non-parallel comparisons set <code>max_parallel_workers_per_gather = 0</code> and <code>jit = off</code>. The parallel counter example also lowers planner costs and thresholds deliberately. Ordinary SQL and the small result totals were separately checked in PGlite 0.5.8, PostgreSQL 18.3/WebAssembly. No production workload was measured.</p>
